{
  "pasos": [
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Class survival"
      },
      "tipo": "mando",
      "dice": {
        "en": "Five sentences will save you in any class. Tap each one: listen, and read what it means. Then I'll put you in trouble!"
      },
      "botones": [
        {
          "es": "¿Cómo se dice … en español?",
          "trad": {
            "en": "How do you say … in Spanish?"
          }
        },
        {
          "es": "¿Cómo se escribe?",
          "trad": {
            "en": "How do you spell it?"
          }
        },
        {
          "es": "¿Qué significa …?",
          "trad": {
            "en": "What does … mean?"
          }
        },
        {
          "es": "No entiendo.",
          "trad": {
            "en": "I don't understand."
          }
        },
        {
          "es": "Más despacio, por favor.",
          "trad": {
            "en": "More slowly, please."
          }
        }
      ],
      "situaciones": [
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "You want to say «table» in Spanish, but you don't know the word."
          },
          "correcta": 0,
          "bien": {
            "en": "**Se dice mesa.** Now you know: «table» is **mesa**."
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "I say «Blablablablabla» at full speed. Much too fast for you!"
          },
          "correcta": 4,
          "cara": "contenta",
          "bien": {
            "en": "Perdona… **Más… des… pa… cio.** Of course!"
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "You hear the word «mesa» and want to write it down. Which letters?"
          },
          "correcta": 1,
          "bien": {
            "en": "**Eme, e, ese, a.** M-e-s-a: mesa."
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "You read «hache» in your book. You have no idea what it is."
          },
          "correcta": 2,
          "bien": {
            "en": "**Hache** significa «the letter h». The silent one!"
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "I explain something long, and you are completely lost."
          },
          "correcta": 3,
          "bien": {
            "en": "No problem! **No entiendo** is the most useful sentence of all."
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "You know what «gracias» means, but not its letters."
          },
          "correcta": 1,
          "bien": {
            "en": "**Ge, erre, a, ce, i, a, ese.** With a **c**, even if it sounds like «th»."
          }
        },
        {
          "pasa": {
            "en": "You need the Spanish word for «please»."
          },
          "correcta": 0,
          "bien": {
            "en": "**Se dice por favor.**"
          }
        }
      ],
      "despues": {
        "en": "With these five sentences you can survive a whole class in Spanish. I mean it."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Class survival"
      },
      "tipo": "reto",
      "bloque": 4,
      "dice": {
        "en": "First check. One of those questions, with a word missing."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Tricky letters"
      },
      "tipo": "explica",
      "dice": {
        "en": "Five letters do not sound the way you expect. This is my sound keyboard: press each key and listen!"
      },
      "palancas": [
        {
          "titulo": {
            "en": "Five surprising letters"
          },
          "posiciones": [
            {
              "etiqueta": "h",
              "es": "**h**ola",
              "trad": {
                "en": "silent! It sounds «O-la»"
              }
            },
            {
              "etiqueta": "j",
              "es": "**j**ota",
              "trad": {
                "en": "a strong, raspy h"
              }
            },
            {
              "etiqueta": "ñ",
              "es": "Espa**ñ**a",
              "trad": {
                "en": "«ny», as in «canyon»"
              }
            },
            {
              "etiqueta": "ll",
              "es": "me **ll**amo",
              "trad": {
                "en": "like «y» in «yes»: «me YA-mo»"
              }
            },
            {
              "etiqueta": "c",
              "es": "gra**c**ias",
              "trad": {
                "en": "in Spain: «th» as in «think» (before e or i)"
              }
            }
          ],
          "retos": [
            {
              "pide": {
                "en": "Listen to a new word. It has the «ny» sound. Which key?"
              },
              "oye": "años",
              "correcta": 2
            },
            {
              "pide": {
                "en": "Listen. This word starts with a letter you cannot hear. Which key?"
              },
              "oye": "hotel",
              "correcta": 0
            },
            {
              "pide": {
                "en": "Listen. It starts with the strong, raspy sound. Which key?"
              },
              "oye": "José",
              "correcta": 1
            },
            {
              "pide": {
                "en": "Listen. In the middle there is a «y» sound, as in «yes». Which key?"
              },
              "oye": "calle",
              "correcta": 3
            },
            {
              "pide": {
                "en": "Listen. In Spain it starts with «th», as in «think». Which key?"
              },
              "oye": "cero",
              "correcta": 4
            }
          ],
          "control": "teclas"
        }
      ],
      "despues": {
        "en": "Now let's see if you can write them. To the blackboard!"
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Tricky letters"
      },
      "tipo": "pizarra",
      "dice": {
        "en": "Now a dictation at the blackboard! One letter is missing. Listen, choose the chalk, and I'll go and write it."
      },
      "palabras": [
        {
          "antes": "",
          "despues": "ola",
          "correcta": "h",
          "opciones": [
            "h",
            "j",
            "y"
          ],
          "oye": "hola",
          "bien": {
            "en": "**hola**: you hear «O-la», but you write the silent **h**."
          },
          "mal": {
            "j": {
              "en": "**j** is a strong, raspy sound. Here you hear nothing at all before the «o»."
            },
            "y": {
              "en": "There is no «y» sound here. You hear «O-la»: the first letter is silent."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "antes": "Espa",
          "despues": "a",
          "correcta": "ñ",
          "opciones": [
            "ñ",
            "n",
            "ny"
          ],
          "oye": "España",
          "bien": {
            "en": "**España**: the **ñ** sounds like «ny» in «canyon». It is a letter of its own."
          },
          "mal": {
            "n": {
              "en": "With **n** it would sound «es-PA-na». Listen: «es-PA-nya»."
            },
            "ny": {
              "en": "It sounds like «ny», yes, but Spanish writes that sound with ONE letter."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "antes": "",
          "despues": "ota",
          "correcta": "j",
          "opciones": [
            "j",
            "h",
            "g"
          ],
          "oye": "jota",
          "bien": {
            "en": "**jota** is the name of the letter **j**: a strong, raspy h."
          },
          "mal": {
            "h": {
              "en": "**h** is silent, and here you hear a strong raspy sound."
            },
            "g": {
              "en": "Close! But the letter that ALWAYS makes this raspy sound is another one."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "antes": "me ",
          "despues": "amo",
          "correcta": "ll",
          "opciones": [
            "ll",
            "y",
            "l"
          ],
          "oye": "me llamo",
          "bien": {
            "en": "**me llamo**: **ll** sounds like the «y» in «yes»."
          },
          "mal": {
            "y": {
              "en": "It sounds like «y», but this word is written with a double letter."
            },
            "l": {
              "en": "One **l** would sound «LA-mo». Listen: «YA-mo»."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "antes": "gra",
          "despues": "ias",
          "correcta": "c",
          "opciones": [
            "c",
            "th",
            "s"
          ],
          "oye": "gracias",
          "bien": {
            "en": "**gracias**: in Spain, **c** before **i** or **e** sounds like «th» in «think»."
          },
          "mal": {
            "th": {
              "en": "It sounds like «th», but Spanish never writes «th»."
            },
            "s": {
              "en": "In Spain this is not an «s» sound. Which letter sounds like «th» before **i**?"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "despues": {
        "en": "Five tricky letters: the silent **h**, the raspy **j**, **ñ**, **ll** and the «th» sound of **c**."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Tricky letters"
      },
      "tipo": "reto",
      "bloque": 7,
      "dice": {
        "en": "Second check. A quick one about letters."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Reading"
      },
      "tipo": "lectura",
      "dice": {
        "en": "Read on your own: no sound, no translation. Lucía and Pablo are in class."
      },
      "titulo": {
        "en": "💬 In class"
      },
      "texto": [
        "Lucía: ¿Cómo se dice «table»?",
        "Pablo: Se dice mesa.",
        "Lucía: Más despacio, por favor.",
        "Pablo: Me-sa. Eme, e, ese, a.",
        "Lucía: ¿Qué significa España?"
      ],
      "preguntas": [
        {
          "pregunta": {
            "en": "What does Lucía want to know first?"
          },
          "opciones": [
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "The word for «table»"
              },
              "correcta": true,
              "explica": {
                "en": "Yes: **¿Cómo se dice…?** asks for the word."
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "Its spelling"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "She asks **¿Cómo se dice…?**: she wants the word itself."
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "Its meaning"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "Meaning is **¿Qué significa…?** Read her first line again."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "pregunta": {
            "en": "Pablo gives her the Spanish word. **Tap the sentence.**"
          },
          "linea": 1,
          "bien": {
            "en": "Yes: **Se dice mesa**, «you say mesa»."
          },
          "mal": {
            "en": "Not that one. Look for **se dice** («you say»)."
          }
        },
        {
          "pregunta": {
            "en": "Why does Lucía say «más despacio»?"
          },
          "opciones": [
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "Pablo is too fast"
              },
              "correcta": true,
              "explica": {
                "en": "Right: **más despacio** = «more slowly»."
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "Pablo is too quiet"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "**Despacio** is about speed, not volume."
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "She wants to go home"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "No! She wants him to slow down: **más despacio**."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "pregunta": {
            "en": "Pablo spells the word. **Tap the sentence.**"
          },
          "linea": 3,
          "bien": {
            "en": "Yes: **eme, e, ese, a** are the names of the letters m, e, s, a."
          },
          "mal": {
            "en": "Not that one. Look for letter names, one by one."
          }
        },
        {
          "pregunta": {
            "en": "What is Lucía's last question about?"
          },
          "opciones": [
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "A meaning"
              },
              "correcta": true,
              "explica": {
                "en": "Yes: **¿Qué significa…?** asks what a word means."
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "A spelling"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "Read the last line: **¿Qué significa…?**"
              }
            },
            {
              "texto": {
                "en": "Pablo's country"
              },
              "explica": {
                "en": "She asks what the word **España** means, not where Pablo is from."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "despues": {
        "en": "You followed a whole class conversation, reading only Spanish."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Reading"
      },
      "tipo": "reto",
      "bloque": 5,
      "dice": {
        "en": "Third check. Pablo's answer, in the right order."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Words"
      },
      "tipo": "letras",
      "dice": {
        "en": "Now you spell. I give you the meaning and you tap the letters in order. A wrong letter and the word comes back later!"
      },
      "palabras": [
        "la mesa",
        "España",
        "por favor",
        "no entiendo",
        "se escribe"
      ],
      "despues": {
        "en": "Letter by letter, and all correct. That is how spelling sticks."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Words"
      },
      "tipo": "reto",
      "bloque": 6,
      "dice": {
        "en": "Last check. Write the whole sentence yourself. Don't forget the accent in **más**."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Off screen"
      },
      "tipo": "mision",
      "bloque": 8,
      "dice": {
        "en": "Last thing, **away from the screen**. I can't check it, so I trust you."
      }
    },
    {
      "etapa": {
        "en": "Off screen"
      },
      "tipo": "fin"
    }
  ]
}
